      "writtenOn": "2022-12-07T21:51:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah yeah, sorry about that. I had originally intended to address this before uploading the CL but forgot to do so.\n\nIn defining valid atomic variable declarations, I wanted to follow WGSL where an atomic type is only allowed in global scope in workgroup storage and inside a writable storage buffer (so having an atomic in a `uniform` block or a `readonly buffer` block would be invalid since atomic builtins that mutate should be disallowed in that case).\n\nI added some enforcement around this now and added test cases for invalid use. PTAL.",
